From 9eb1e32c8dda2b6d9d8825aed33f251d64946d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:01:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] pm: resolve seed account from passwd under a fake
 HOME

A clean env -i HOME=<scratch> run made account_home_root compare the
scratch data root with itself, disabling cache/tool/source borrowing and
lazy bytecode. Reuse account_default_hermes_home, the existing passwd-backed
platform/suffix resolver, without changing samefile/device/opt-out gates.
Keep PM and shared admission fixtures isolated from the real account.
Desktop build bootstraps explicitly opt out: their caches and dependency
state must remain build-owned rather than borrowing the invoking account.

Proof: default/canary no-HERMES_HOME regressions RED on 29944b5086e8,
GREEN after. Clean real fake-HOME run of test_account_seed.py measured
570431093 -> 14156475 private logical bytes and 629051392 -> 16924672
allocated bytes. Full inode accounting counts all links inside the home,
not only nlink==1. After has 8272 inodes shared with the account uv cache;
fresh test-environment native extensions match those cache inodes.
Real-account path/inode probe fails on base and passes with the fix.

Audited _account_seed, account_environment/_snapshot_donor and
PythonEnvironment._compile_bytecode; they inherit the corrected root.
